Give the gyp-built shared libraries a $ORIGIN runpath.

The coreconf build added -Wl,-z,origin -Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN through DSO_LDOPTS so
each nss library finds its siblings in the same directory. The gyp build never
reads the coreconf makefiles, so add the same link flags to the shared library
settings in config.gypi. The \$$ORIGIN spelling is how gyp's own ninja
generator escapes a literal $ORIGIN. The flags apply only where GNU ld is used.

--- nss/nss/coreconf/config.gypi
+++ nss/nss/coreconf/config.gypi
@@ -329,6 +329,8 @@
           [ 'cc_use_gnu_ld==1', {
             'ldflags': [
               '-Wl,--gc-sections',
+              '-Wl,-z,origin',
+              '-Wl,-rpath=\\$$ORIGIN',
             ],
             'conditions': [
               ['no_zdefs==0', {
